OK, I'll take the bait. I play ASCII for two reasons:

(1) I haven't found a tileset that is (to me) esthetically
pleasing; and, more importantly,

(2) ASCII motivates imagining the surroundings. (Yes, I like wandering
about/semicoloning in an armor shop. This is the only good way I can
"see" a really[1] impressive crystal plate mail, etc.)

NB: The only way you can spoil your ASCII experience is by using
IBM/DEC Graphics. (OTOH, their style reminds me of some funny memories
of the good time I had once finding out which key combinations
produced smileys on my father's PC. 'Twas the first (and only) use I
saw in computers some 18 years ago.)

[1] Esthetics by underspecification. The other way to achieve it is
cutting on perceptiveness, e.g. by playing NetHack drunk (in this case
you can use tiles.)

